  "scope": "Registry: the whole unchanged server booted as oracle/world-trace boots it (boot record byte-identical to the world-trace fixture, two fresh JVM runs identical); CommandMapping in getNames() order with each command's name, privilege, usage, description and handler class, the legacy CommandSet plugin lists and getPageIndices(0..3). Behaviour: on JDK 11 with Kotlin 1.8.20, each case in a fresh class loader, the unchanged Command, CommandSystem, CommandPlugin, CommandSet (legacy enum), Privilege, sets.CommandSet, ModerationCommandSet, SystemCommandSet, TeleportCommandSet, PlayerAttributeCommandSet, AbuseReport, Rule, QCRepository, QuickChatPacketHandler, Packet, ChatMessage, Rights, UserAccountInfo, EquipmentSlot, InputType, Globals, StringUtils, IoBuffer, PacketHeader, IncomingPacket, ISAACCipher, ByteBufferUtils, Plugin, Initializable and proto.management; original text inserted: the COMMAND, REPORT_ABUSE and QUICKCHAT decoders and Decoders530.process, the Command, ReportAbuse and QuickChat branches of PacketProcessor.process, ServerConstants.TELEPORT_DESTINATIONS, Player/PlayerDetails.getRights, Skills.SKILL_NAME/getSkillByName/getExperienceByLevel and the Log enum. Recording adapters: the repository name map, account storage and authenticator, ServerStore, the pulse runner (pulses, tasks, input handlers and the csvmodcr coroutine are kept and run by later operations), messages, chat, dialogues, zones, PlayerMonitor, teleports, attributes, containers and items, ChargedItem, the system manager, the cache index 24 files, data maps, item definitions, skills, slayer, clans, the management queue, the chat mask and Discord. The four sets register in the scan order; three legacy plugins are linked to ADMINISTRATOR as the boot links the originals; content commands are case-registered stand-ins. Wall clock reads are recorded case inputs (tool/Rewrite.java of the social oracle). Not driven: ::shutdown (exitProcess), Rule.canRequest, the Spawn, Stats, Misc and development sets and the content command bodies.",
